<!--
    The callee clause of `option argclobber`: a callee that READS the argument
    register before writing it keeps its argument, whatever the caller's side
    looks like.

    The caller here is byte-for-byte the shape the option is FOR, the same one
    tests/stages/kuna-argclobber.xml drops: one path calls `clobber` (which
    destroys rdx and whose own first act is a call, so `calleepreserves` cannot
    narrow the killed set), the other leaves an `idivl` remainder in edx while
    using only the quotient, and the two join at the call.  Every incoming value
    for rdx is therefore one the caller did not put there for this call, and the
    only difference from the positive fixture is the callee:

        reader: mov %rdx, %rax ; ret

    The caller-side evidence cannot tell this apart from the phantom, and the
    callee settles it: bytes it reads at entry are a parameter however the
    value got into the register. `calleedeadarg` already decodes each callee
    once per image for the opposite claim (does it overwrite the register
    before reading it?), so this reads the same summary's `proves_input` half.

    This is the clause that answers for a callee kuna never recovered as
    variadic. u-boot -O2 `sub_60873270` is printf, called from 1,924 sites, and
    its prologue spilling r1-r3 into the va_list save area settles every one of
    them at once.

    WHY THIS PASSES NOW.  This fixture predates the recovered-prototype rule and
    pins its clause against the CALLER's side.  Under the current rule the
    decisive statement is the callee's own recovered prototype, which reaches a
    call site only through `protoorder`, and this harness decompiles ONE
    function from a byte image: no callee was decompiled first, nothing is
    stated, and the drop is declined before any caller-side clause is reached
    (the same blanket decline tests/stages/kuna-argclobber.xml pins).  So the
    pass-2 survival here is that decline, not the clause described above.  The
    clause is kept in prose because it still runs wherever a prototype IS
    stated, and the live coverage of the rule on a real image is in tests/cli/
    (argclobber-drops-a-trailing-clobbered-argument.json and its off arm,
    argclobber-keeps-the-jump-table-callees-argument.json).

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 "active-input-trial-scoring".  Both passes must
    render the same three-argument call, so the assertion counts 2.
-->
